{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788481852079705002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"forgetful-smellable-myotis","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"8da9592509f41bfb2fd9e01ae1ae00454bea62a49f6ffc106cedf3f0ce2dced2","event_uuid":"e7e2a994-8d48-44a1-acd1-42b418609b88","position":{"commit_sha":"0d6254b9b2d121c0e7cfca80b92f86d1fd1b7cc7","position":"1788479767040363001-e7e2a994-8d48-44a1-acd1-42b418609b88"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"91f0a2ce0b272930c61b7e35bec0d2928e9e57c78aac319be9a727210049f151","event_uuid":"255dfc11-ec68-4388-a364-c16ed7f3a962","position":{"commit_sha":"4dd255e2116f5ce925ef7b84339daed2f2f0665f","position":"1788479778238019001-255dfc11-ec68-4388-a364-c16ed7f3a962"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"37de2db4a147110307ac325e15aad7105abffdd1d48378156f11040a2896b636","event_uuid":"86d2e39b-feac-49e0-8220-3fb3c8d0019a","position":{"commit_sha":"c6ecf556c75a0f25e260bb9496cf8a84fc42a534","position":"1788480843596917001-86d2e39b-feac-49e0-8220-3fb3c8d0019a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"33e28f260de5fa422a1be8bdec600a5e0b7f34de4aa865a38dee5230ea4926ae","event_uuid":"b61bb540-875a-4b88-a769-cbbdea5f7083","position":{"commit_sha":"6f89dd9584e81cc55b7d498315089a38935d861e","position":"1788481306312364001-b61bb540-875a-4b88-a769-cbbdea5f7083"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"adc26fdbfbade8abc194d5f910f074a45fb0e2478e46ea72a6b3e8fa5681976c","event_uuid":"33464fae-500e-40cb-9dee-7d35f6499664","position":{"commit_sha":"5ed9a7aee68b37bd60a0f2ab9c98593bf1cc58cf","position":"1788481852079705001-33464fae-500e-40cb-9dee-7d35f6499664"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Post-compaction cycle: split stack triaged, one landed, harness bug filed\n\n**Landed.** Change 2596 (split jira/acli.py REST issue ops into acli_rest.py) reached\nLLM-Review +1 / Verified +1 and is now MERGED on main. Note for future submits: Gerrit's\nPOST /a/changes/<n>/submit requires a JSON body -- sending only the Content-Type header\nreturns HTTP 400 \"Expected JSON object\" and the change silently stays NEW. Use -d '{}'.\nMy first attempt failed this way and I only caught it by re-reading the change status.\n\n**The three Verified -1 changes were not one problem.** Triage separated them:\n\n- 2593 (split plan_review/sizing.py): a REAL failure -- the architecture-invariant test\n  test_review_discovery_architecture pinned a hard-coded list of discovery-projection\n  builder modules, and the split moved the DiscoveryStagePlan construction into the new\n  checkpoints.py. Fixed and re-pushed as patchset 2 (4e8983dbfb4f). The fix went further\n  than repointing the list: the builder set is now DERIVED from the tree by scanning\n  src/rebar/llm for stage constructions (the same pattern the sibling\n  test_no_second_discovery_scheduler_outside_the_kernel already uses), with a retained\n  anti-vanish half asserting each gate package still owns a seam. Proven with three RED\n  plants -- a violation in the moved builder, a violation in a brand-new module (which the\n  old hard-coded list passed SILENTLY), and the seam vanishing. Same builder set as before,\n  strictly larger reach.\n\n- 2594 (split _commands/composer.py): NOT caused by the change. Pre-existing harness race.\n- 2595 (pin review scanner contracts): not mine, already set WIP by another session, and\n  failing on all three Python versions -- a different signature from the single-worker\n  crash. Left alone.\n- 2592 (docs: prohibit internal-only shims): not mine; patchset 2 at LLM-Review +1, CI running.\n\n**New orphan bug filed: 9a17-e0b3-7aa6-4091 / skipping-unamorous-massasauga.**\nTwo independent subagents converged on the same root cause with the same evidence, which is\nwhy this was filed as a bug rather than retried. The e2e session-scoped bpmn_harness fixture\nprovisions the Node toolchain lazily INSIDE the first e2e test's setup (npm install at\nconftest.py:51, npm run build at :57, neither carrying an explicit timeout= unlike every\nother subprocess in that file). That cost is charged against timeout=300 with\ntimeout_method=\"thread\" and deliberately no timeout_func_only, and the thread method calls\nos._exit(1) -- so it kills the xdist worker instead of reporting Failed: Timeout. The\nmechanism is already documented in-tree at .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:773-775.\nMeasured in a PASSING run: 101.26s / 120.93s / 89.69s of a 300s budget, a 2.5-3.3x margin.\nCI has no setup-node step and no npm cache. Observed on 2592, 2593, 2594; absent on 2596.\nLinked discovered_from the janitor epic 78f2 / equitable-snazzy-fruitfly, file_impact set.\n\nAC5 is deliberately a REAL-TIME verification per the standing rule that time-dependent\nacceptance criteria are defective: run the suite cold under the CI xdist configuration and\nobserve no worker kill, then stub npm to stall past the new explicit timeout and assert the\nresult is the named diagnosable failure rather than \"node down\". Both complete in one run --\nno waiting for a flake to recur.\n\nPosted an honest recheck on 2594 stating this is a known pre-existing harness race with a\nticket, NOT an infra flake. Per AGENTS.md a flaky test is root-caused rather than retried;\nthe root cause is captured in 9a17, so the recheck unblocks this unrelated change rather\nthan papering over the defect. Confirmed from CONTRIBUTING.md that \"recheck\" is the CI\ntrigger and shares no substring with \"rerun-llm-review\" by design.\n\n**ADR number collision, second occurrence.** Epic 6202's draft ADR claimed 0111, but change\n2592 has already claimed docs/adr/0111-no-internal-only-compatibility-shims.md AND the\ndocs/adr/.numbers/0111 reservation marker, and is further along (LLM-Review +1, CI running).\nCI script scripts/check_adr_numbers.py asserts a bijection between marker files and ADR\nfiles, so this would have failed the gate. Ours renumbers to 0112. This is the second\ncollision after 0110 -- the reservation marker is only created when the ADR is authored, so\ntwo agents drafting concurrently will keep colliding. Worth a mechanism ticket if it recurs.\n\n**Epic identity correction.** The draft ADR cited \"epic livid-blondish-shearwater\n(7dfa-18ca-9c04-4691)\" -- that is wrong. 7dfa IS story S0, the ADR's own ticket. The epic is\n6202-e1c7-c57f-4897 / endowed-upset-scaup, \"Bounded disk-ceiling architecture for the Gerrit\nhost\". Being fixed alongside the renumber.\n\n**Also being corrected in the ADR:** my own earlier overstatement that ADRs 0079 and 0104\n\"decided the box stays t4g.large\" as a standing prohibition. Their actual claim is narrow\nand memory-scoped -- that the transient 2x container memory during MCP deploy overlap never\nforces the t4g.large up to a t4g.xlarge. Neither says anything about root volume size.\nThe ADR must decline a resize on its own reasoning, not by leaning on a constraint those\nADRs do not impose.\n\n**Board:** 3 orphan bugs in_progress (3276, 9ea3, bff5), 2 orphan bugs open and untriaged\n(740d brunette-bellicose-blacklemur, 9a17 skipping-unamorous-massasauga). Epic 6202\nin_progress; S0 (7dfa) still open, awaiting the renumber before its plan review.","timestamp":1788479778238019001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## S0 landed for review as ADR 0112; a shared-checkout ownership finding\n\n**S0 (7dfa / livid-blondish-shearwater) passed plan review, claimed, committed, pushed as\nGerrit change 2598.** The ADR is docs/adr/0112-on-box-disk-ceiling-architecture.md.\n\n**The first plan-review run BLOCKED, correctly, on something I had missed.** The single\nblocking finding (criterion G7) was parent/child divergence: I had renumbered the child ADR\ntwice (0110 -> 0111 -> 0112) but never propagated either correction UP to the parent epic,\nwhich still named docs/adr/0110-gerrit-disk-ceiling-architecture.md in its AC1, its \"ADR draft\nlocation\" note, and its file_impact. So the epic promised 0110 while the story delivered 0112.\nFixed by updating the epic's description and all 12 file_impact paths. This is a failure mode\nworth checking proactively on ANY renumber or rename -- a leaf correction that silently leaves\nthe parent stale -- rather than waiting for a gate to catch it.\n\nThe re-run PASSED with zero blocking findings and one minor advisory (2 acceptance-criterion\nlines bundle deliverables with \"and\"). Left as-is rather than churning the attestation after\nthe claim.\n\nAlso corrected the ROOT of the whole collision chain, which was in S0's own research section:\nthe plan asserted \"highest current number is 0109\" when 0110 had already landed in commit\n8f19115cf2fb. Because the .numbers/ reservation marker is only created when an ADR is\nAUTHORED, any plan that reads the highest number at planning time is stale by landing time.\nTwo concurrent drafters will keep colliding. If it happens a third time, that is a mechanism\nproblem deserving its own ticket.\n\n**Commit-message gate detail worth remembering:** the pre-commit hook enforces a 50-char\nsubject and 72-column body wrap (Gerrit renders the description as preformatted text).\nTrailers, URLs, table rows and fenced code are exempt. My first attempt was rejected on six\nlong lines and an over-length subject; the fix is to wrap, not to bypass.\n\n**Shared-checkout ownership finding (asked by the user).** The primary checkout at\n/Users/joeoakhart/rebar currently holds 14 MODIFIED source files that are NOT this session's:\nan LLM / code-review / reconciler cluster (_mcp_llm.py, llm/code_review/shim.py,\n_cli/_llm_commands.py, _cli/_parsers/advanced/llm.py, _engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py,\n_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py plus their tests, including test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py),\ntimestamped 02:51-07:21 today in two or three distinct bursts. Verified these are NOT Gerrit\nchange 2592's despite the shared \"shim\" theme -- 2592 touches only docs/api-stability.md,\ndocs/architecture.md, two test files and the 0111 ADR trio. So a third session has uncommitted\nwork there. LEFT STRICTLY ALONE. All of this session's code work has been in worktrees.\n\n**But one untracked file in that checkout WAS ours, and it was a mistake.** The subagent\ndriving bug 9a17 ran its plan review from the repo ROOT and redirected output to\n`.rp-9a17.log` there. Two problems: it littered a checkout holding another session's WIP, and\n-- more seriously -- that run used the stale global pipx rebar, whose own warning reads \"this\nrebar build (cdfd7d94d, 2026-08-29, dirty) is 195 commit(s) BEHIND the ref this gate pinned\n(08a39c39c) ... results can be wrong in ways the verdict cannot show\". AGENTS.md requires the\nrepo checkout's build when developing rebar itself. Messaged the subagent to create its\nworktree FIRST, re-run the gate from inside it with the worktree venv on PATH, confirm `which\nrebar` resolves there before trusting any verdict, and remove only that one stray file.\n\nContrast: the S0 gate runs used `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\"` from the worktree and\nreported only \"1 commit BEHIND\" -- the correct posture. **The venv-on-PATH rule is not just\nabout the commit hook finding ruff/mypy; it also determines which rebar BUILD evaluates a\ngate.** A subagent brief should say so explicitly, because the failure is silent.\n\n**Gerrit now:** 2593 (sizing split) LLM+1, CI re-running after patchset 2. 2594 (composer\nsplit) LLM+1, CI re-running after the recheck. 2598 (ADR 0112) awaiting both votes.\n2596 (acli split) MERGED and now the tip of origin/main at 08a39c39c50d.\n\n**Board:** 3 orphan bugs in_progress (3276, 9ea3, bff5), 2 orphan bugs dispatched to subagents\n(740d triage-only; 9a17 full cycle). Epic 6202 in_progress, S0 in_progress, S6 next -- it is\nthe precondition for S2-S5 because the janitor reclaims by high-water mark over\ndelete-on-last-close, so a cap below peak concurrent hold cannot be honoured by reclamation.","timestamp":1788480843596917001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## 740d triage reversed a recorded disposition -- it is a genuine defect\n\nThe ticket carried two prior RCA comments concluding 'host-environment artifact, no code fix\nwarranted'. That is wrong, and the project's own history settles it without needing a judgement call.\n\nRoot cause: git refuses to DISCOVER a bare repo via -C/cwd when safe.bareRepository=explicit; it\naccepts one named by top-level --git-dir. The _git helper in\ntests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py:40-46 hardcodes git -C <repo>, so the five\ntests reading the bare fixture remote die with exit 128 BEFORE any ref lookup.\n\nTwo claims in the original report are false and were sending readers down dead ends:\n - 'refs/heads/tickets does not exist' -- it exists and resolves fine; git never gets that far.\n - 'git 2.55.0' -- safe.bareRepository shipped in git 2.38.0 (2022-10-03) with exactly these\n   semantics. Four years stable. No version regression to chase.\n\nMeasured: 17 passed under default config isolated; 546 passed across the whole lifecycle directory;\n5 failed / 12 passed under safe.bareRepository=explicit. No pollution, no ordering dependency -- one\nconfig value governs the split entirely. Reproduced with an ordinary user gitconfig, no\nGIT_CONFIG_COUNT injection, so it is not a harness artifact.\n\nWHY IT IS A RECURRENCE, AND THE PART THAT MATTERS: closed ticket 3476-4472-3407-4246\n(embolismic-adverse-dragon) fixed this exact class across 13 files and added the held-out oracle\ntests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py. It also recorded the policy\nverbatim: 'the supported test suite must run both locally and in CI. Treat agents dismissing\nreproducible local test failures as environmental noise as an anti-pattern.' The guard missed this\nfile because it pins a HARDCODED 3-entry _FIXTURE_NODES allowlist, and\ntest_atomic_completion_close.py landed 2026-08-25 (commit 1cb1cdd25aff) -- four days after the guard\nand three days before 3476 closed. No static sweep exists anywhere (scripts/, Makefile,\n.pre-commit-config.yaml); scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py covers an unrelated concern.\n\nSo fixing only the five call sites would leave exactly the gap that produced this recurrence. AC4\ntherefore targets the allowlist itself: the guard's coverage must be derived from the tree, or an\nunregistered bare-fixture test must fail. This is the same lesson as the 2593 fix, where a\nhard-coded module list was replaced by a tree-derived scan -- twice in one day a hand-maintained\nallowlist silently stopped guarding.\n\nTicket retitled around safe.bareRepository=explicit, description rewritten with the measurements,\nfile_impact set to the two files, linked relates_to 3476, and the disposition correction recorded as\na comment. Fix subagent dispatched with both halves required and AC3's mutation proof mandatory.\n\nCROSS-CUTTING LESSON now in every subagent brief: putting the worktree venv first on PATH is not\nonly about the commit hook resolving ruff/mypy -- it also determines WHICH REBAR BUILD evaluates a\ngate. The global pipx rebar on this host is ~195 commits stale and its verdicts 'can be wrong in\nways the verdict cannot show'. Briefs now require confirming 'which rebar' resolves into the\nworktree and reading the gate's own build_drift line before trusting a verdict.","timestamp":1788481306312364001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## The stale global rebar was not normal -- the hourly updater has been dead for 119 runs\n\nThe user asked whether this environment has an auto-update keeping rebar in sync with origin/main.\nIt does, and it is BROKEN. I had treated the 195-commits-behind global build as an ambient fact and\nmerely routed around it; it is actually a five-day outage of the update mechanism, affecting every\nsession on this host.\n\nFiled ae97-a37b-9fa3-413a / princely-courageous-milksnake, priority 1.\n\nROOT CAUSE -- an inverted assumption, not a missing upgrade.\nrebar-dev-update.sh:18 hardcodes UV_BIN=${REBAR_DEV_UV_BIN:-/opt/homebrew/bin/uv}, and :120 orders\nPATH to keep Homebrew authoritative with the stated reason at :116-118: 'Keep Homebrew before\n~/.local/bin so the obsolete standalone uv there cannot shadow the pinned UV_BIN.' Measured today:\n/opt/homebrew/bin/uv is 0.12.6 (2026-08-25); /Users/joeoakhart/.local/bin/uv is 0.12.7 (2026-08-27).\nThe premise inverted -- Homebrew is now the stale side -- so the guard written to prevent selecting\na stale uv is the mechanism selecting one. pyproject.toml:346 pins required-version = '==0.12.7',\nuv reads it itself and fails fast, so every hourly 'uv sync' aborts. 118 of 119 rejections are this;\none is a transient fetch-pack early EOF at the checkout stage.\n\nSAME PIN, THIRD CONSUMER. required-version '==0.12.7' (commit 7501cc1d602d) is the same pin whose\nfloating uv:latest Dockerfile tags caused the multi-hour MCP outage under bug febd. That fix pinned\nthe three infra/compose Dockerfiles and extended scripts/check_uv_pin.py to scan them. This host's\nupdater is a third consumer that was never brought along -- and it is out of check_uv_pin.py's reach\nbecause it is a machine-local, git-ignored script. Linked relates_to febd.\n\nTHE DETECTION GAP IS THE WORSE HALF. docs/local-env-main-tracking.local.md documents a\nREJECT_STREAK_ALERT (default 3) added after 'the b477339a99 incident: 43 hourly sync rejections,\n~48 commits behind, no signal'. That alert is firing correctly every hour and failing to deliver\nevery time: AuthorizationError, IAM user in account 820258254566 publishing to an SNS topic in\naccount 896586841071, no resource-based policy permitting it. Streak 119 against a threshold of 3,\nzero operator signal -- a strictly worse recurrence of the exact incident the alert exists to\nprevent. So AC4 requires a LOCAL detector that does not depend on the remote sink at all.\n\nIMPACT WORTH BEING BLUNT ABOUT: any plan-review or completion-verifier verdict produced through the\nglobal rebar on this host in the last five days used a build whose own advisory says results 'can\nbe wrong in ways the verdict cannot show'. That is not limited to this session.\n\nSecondary: launchd.err.log shows the pruner failing with 'Directory not empty' on release dirs, and\nreleases/5fb693345b0c...1559 is a 3-entry stub from a partially built release. At ~346 MB per\nrelease dir this is disk-ceiling relevant, so linked relates_to epic 6202.\n\nCORRECTION TO MY OWN EARLIER FRAMING: I told a subagent to use the worktree venv 'because the global\nbuild is stale'. That was the right instruction for the wrong reason -- I presented a broken\nupdater as a standing environmental condition. The venv-on-PATH rule remains correct regardless,\nbut the staleness itself is a bug with a ticket, not a fact of the environment.","timestamp":1788481852079705001}],"created_at":1788479767040363001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ebce-3f69-71a0-417f","ticket_type":"session_log","title":"Session log","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e7e2a994-8d48-44a1-acd1-42b418609b88","255dfc11-ec68-4388-a364-c16ed7f3a962","86d2e39b-feac-49e0-8220-3fb3c8d0019a","b61bb540-875a-4b88-a769-cbbdea5f7083","33464fae-500e-40cb-9dee-7d35f6499664"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788481852079705002,"uuid":"1612f173-0250-4093-a4b7-fa39af3a0b96"}